  "body": "The review of PR #3185 (comment 7069026569) found three items that do not block it. They are owed polish.\n\n1. `.github/scripts/post-merge-report.sh:54-60`: when `gh issue view` fails, `issue_body` gives an empty string (`|| true`). Then `set_marker` replaces the full issue body with only the marker. The list of red steps of the first red run is lost. Keep the body when the read fails, or skip the marker write.\n2. `.github/scripts/post-merge-report.sh:41`: the search for the newest issue takes the first result and gives no sort order. Use `$open` first, or add `sort:created-desc` to the search.\n3. `.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md` still says \"A group of merges tests only the newest head\". After PR #3185, each merge gets its own run. Change the skill text. This is a process file, so the PR body needs the line `Process change: yes`.\n\nThe `order::*` tests in `xtask/tests/post_merge_report.rs` are `#[cfg(unix)]`. They did not run on the Windows review machine. A Linux run of `cargo test -p xtask --test post_merge_report` confirms them.\n",
